---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { components, slug, title } from '../lib/manifest';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base title="Vastu" description="A small design system of Lit web components that agents can use and test.">
  <h1>Vastu</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A small design system of web components, built with Lit. Every promise it makes, from its API and keyboard
    behaviour to its theming hooks and usage guidance, is written once in a machine-readable manifest. Docs, agent
    tools and tests are all generated from that one description.
  </p>
  <p>
    The name comes from Vastu Shastra, the ancient Indian science of space, layout and proportion. This site shows the
    first brand, <strong>Lekha</strong>. Switch between light, dark and high-contrast modes at the top of the page.
  </p>

  <h2>Components</h2>
  <ul class="cards">
    {
      components.map((c) => (
        <li>
          <a href={`${base}components/${slug(c.tagName)}/`}>
            <strong>{title(c.tagName)}</strong>
            <code>&lt;{c.tagName}&gt;</code>
          </a>
          <p>{c.summary}</p>
          <div class="preview" set:html={c['x-examples'][0].code} />
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h2>Status</h2>
  <p>
    Milestone M1: eight components, each checked on every change by contract tests generated from the manifest,
    behaviour tests, axe accessibility checks in every mode, visual regression at phone and desktop widths, size budgets,
    and a strict Content Security Policy with Trusted Types, in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit. Next is the agent layer: a
    markup validator, an MCP server and an eval. Read the
    <a href="https://github.com/firstprateek/vastu/blob/main/docs/design.md">design document</a>.
  </p>
</Base>

<script>
  import '@firstprateek/vastu/all';
</script>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  .cards {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr));
  }
  .cards li {
    border: 1px solid var(--va-color-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--va-radius-surface);
    padding: 16px;
  }
  .cards a {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 8px;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .preview {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--va-font-family-ui);
  }
  .cards p {
    margin: 8px 0 12px;
    color: var(--va-color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
</style>
